# CoW Track 1A (remediation-2) — `(&a).enumerate()` receiver-wrap writes through.
#
# The `&` can land on the RECEIVER of `.enumerate()` instead of the statement:
# `for i, x in (&a).enumerate():` must behave identically to
# `for i, x in &a.enumerate():` (§3.1 — same unbroken `&` chain, spelled with
# parens). Pins the shape where the first remediation introduced a cross-lane
# divergence (Rust stripped the receiver wrap; the self-host probe did not →
# Rust `101` vs self-host `1`). All three `&` spellings now share one strip
# path per lane.
# Output must be correct on BOTH backends.

struct Cell:
    int v

void main():
    Vector[Cell] a = [Cell(1)]
    for i, x in (&a).enumerate():
        x.v = x.v + 100 + i
    print(a.get(0).unwrap().v)
